nnovation defines everything they do. Iron Mountain Incorporated was founded in 1951 and is incorporated in Delaware and is based in Portsmouth, New Hampshire.","ceo_bio":"Mr. William L. Meaney BSc, MEng, MSIA | President, CEO & Director | Age 65 | Compensation: $3.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 29K people. Revenue per employee of $235K ranks in the bottom quartile among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 5%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 15\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Iron Mountain Incorporated (Del is a large-cap real estate business with a $33.9B market cap on $6.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $932M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 7.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $21.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["16 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Price-Driven Insight from (IRM) for Rule-Based Strategy","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/151/Price-Driven_Insight_from_IRM_for_Rule-Based_Strategy_111226012002_1794464402.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794464402.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Iron Mountain (NYSE:IRM) Leasing Record Data Center Space?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/infrastructure-and-real-estate/is-iron-mountain-nyseirm-leasing-record-data-center-space","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794402600.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.625,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Iron Mountain (IRM) Raises Outlook And Dividend, Is The Stock Still Undervalued?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-irm/iron-mountain/news/iron-mountain-irm-raises-outlook-and-dividend-is-the-stock-s","d