ree rate) and an EBIT/EV of 2.1% (vs the 8% bar).","The 11 covering analysts target $139 on average, 22% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 7% falls short of the cost of capital of 7.9%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have been steady (CV 0.23).","It burns cash (FCF margin -13%).","AFFO margin (a proxy for distributable REIT cash) is -13%.","It spends 2.0% of revenue on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 7.4x net debt to EBITDA ($158.5M of cash against $16.4B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 1.4x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 1.39 in the distress zone.","The current ratio of 0.74 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 10.6% over 3 years, 10.7% over 5 years and 8.7% over 10 years.","At current returns, reinvesting 100% of profits supports about 6.6% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Forward indicators: a backlog worth 0% of annual revenue, deferred revenue up 30% and FFO growth of 6.3% a year over five years.","Capex runs 2.2x depreciation (32.9% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is -5, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.9%), and institutions hold 86%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (20 sales, net $21.5M sold).","It returns 2.7% a year to shareholders (3.5% in dividends).","The share count has grown 0.5% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","It pays out 226% of earnings, more than it earns, so the dividend is at risk."],"people":["With about 29,400 employees, each generates about $235K of revenue, 0.1x the Real Estate median, and revenue has grown 5.4% a year across its filed history.","Free cash flow is negative, at -$32K per employee.","CEO pay is $3.5M (15x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $5K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INSUFFICIENT DATA","conv":null,"head":"Not enough